(a) whether the standards for road design, construction and maintenance, and other matters under Section 198A of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 have been prescribed by the Central Government and, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the State-wise/UT-wise number of complaints, prosecutions, convictions and penalties under the said provision since its commencement;
(c) the year-wise amount recovered as penalties and credited to the Motor Vehicle Accident Fund under Section 164B; and
(d) the steps taken to implement and monitor the enforcement of Section 198A across the country?

(a) whether Government has taken note that three official reports published in 2026, namely the Ministry’s Road Accidents in India 2024, NCRB’s Accidental Deaths and Suicides in India 2024, and NCRB’s Crime in India 2024, which provides different figures for road deaths in the same year, with a variation of nearly 6,000 lives;
(b) the reasons for such variation and the steps taken to reconcile these figures; and
(c) whether Government proposes to establish a unified and independently verified national road-crash database?

(a) the percentage of farmers who sold their Paddy and Wheat at the announced Minimum Support Price through Government procurement during marketing seasons in the last five years, State-wise;
(b) the total value of foodgrains procured under MSP-linked procurement during the same period and the State-wise breakdown thereof; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the percentage of small and marginal farmers - as a proportion of all farmers who are actually able to access MSP procurement?

(a) the total value of India's merchandise imports from China during each of the last five financial years;
(b) the percentage share of imports from China in India's total merchandise imports during the said period;
(c) the value of India's imports from the ten largest import partner countries during each of the last five financial years, indicating China's rank among them; and
(d) the trade deficit between India and China during each of the last five financial years?

(a) the number of cases under the SC and ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 that have reached the High Courts and the Supreme Court by way of appeal, revision, transfer petition since the said Act was enacted, year-wise;
(b) the number of such cases in which the judgment of trial court has been affirmed, modified, set aside by the appellate courts;
(c) the average time taken for disposal of such cases by the High Courts and the Supreme Court; and
(d) whether Government maintains data regarding movement and disposal of cases under the Act across different levels of judicial system and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has examined the reasons for the continued occurrence of deaths during sewer and septic tank cleaning despite the statutory prohibition on hazardous manual cleaning; 
(b) the number of cases registered under the relevant provisions of the Prohibition of Employment as Manual Scavengers and their Rehabilitation Act, 2013, the Indian Penal Code & other applicable laws in relation to such deaths during the last five years, State-wise; and
(c) the details of persons, agencies and authorities held responsible in such cases, including contractors, municipal corporations, urban local bodies, Government Departments, private agencies, supervisors and officials responsible for permitting hazardous cleaning work?

(a) whether Government has examined the concerns that deaths occurring during sewer and septic tank cleaning are not uniformly recorded as deaths due to manual scavenging due to definitional limitations under the Prohibition of Employment as Manual Scavengers and their Rehabilitation Act, 2013;
(b) whether Government proposes to revise the definition or create a separate national category for "sewer and septic tank cleaning deaths" to ensure accurate reporting and accountability; and
(c) whether a national database of all sanitation-related occupational deaths is proposed to be created and if so, the details thereof?

(a) total number of beneficiaries currently covered under the Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY) category of the National Food Security Act, 2013, State-wise;
(b) number of AAY households with five or more members, State-wise, who currently receive the flat 35 kg per household per month entitlement;
(c) number of AAY households that would receive less than 35 kg per month under the proposed 7 kg per person per month formula proposed in the draft National Food Security (Amendment) Bill, 2026; and
(d) whether any nutritional impact assessment has been carried out before proposing this change, if so, the agency name?

(a) whether NITI Aayog has measured the divergence in per-capita income between the poorest and richest States over the last decade and Bihar’s position therein;
(b) the specific instruments in the Viksit Bharat 2047 framework for accelerated convergence of lagging States, beyond Finance Commission devolution;
(c) the outcome ranking of Bihar’s 13 Aspirational Districts on health, nutrition and education indicators since inception; and
(d) whether NITI Aayog has examined the case for a formal special assistance framework for low-income, high-population States whose demographic weight will drive the national workforce until 2047?

(a) the total number of sanctioned posts in Indian Railways and the number of vacancies as on the latest available date, disaggregated by safety-critical categories- loco pilots, assistant loco pilots, station masters, signal maintainers and trackmen;
(b) the recruitment made through the Railway Recruitment Boards in each of the last five years, against the annual recruitment target, year-wise;
(c) the number of candidates who have cleared Railway Recruitment Board examinations in the last three years but have not received appointment orders; and
(d) the reasons for delay in issuing appointment orders and the expected timeline for completing these pending appointments?

(a) the all-India rural current weekly status unemployment rate, as per the latest Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS); 
(b) the youth (age 15-29) unemployment rate in rural India as per the same survey; 
(c) whether youth unemployment in rural India remains in double digits; 
(d) the trend in this youth unemployment figure during the last five PLFS cycles; and 
(e) the specific employment-generation schemes, with budget allocation, targeted at reducing rural youth unemployment during 2025-26?

(a) the current national floor level minimum wage as notified under the Code on Wages, 2026 and how it compares to the national floor minimum wage in each year from 2021-22 to 2025-26;
(b) the number of States where the state-notified minimum wage is currently below the national floor level minimum wage;
(c) the number of minimum wage violation cases registered under the new labour law framework in each month from November 2025 to May 2026; and
(d) the number of workers in enterprises employing fewer than ten workers who remain largely outside the ambit of the Labour Codes as a proportion of India's total workforce, based on the most recent available data?

vg

(a) the total number of cases registered under the SC and ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 in Uttar Pradesh in each year from 2019 to 2024, as reported by National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB);
(b) the conviction rate in cases registered under this Act in Uttar Pradesh in each of these years, compared to the national average conviction rate for the same years; and
(c) the total compensation disbursed to victims of caste atrocities in Uttar Pradesh under the SC and ST (Prevention of Atrocities) Act in each of the last five financial years, against the amount sanctioned?

(a) the total number of beneficiaries currently covered under free foodgrain distribution schemes in rural areas;
(b) whether this number has increased, decreased or remained unchanged over the last five years;
(c) whether any State Government has requested a reduction in allocation citing improved rural household incomes; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the continuing dependence on free foodgrain support, if so, whether it is consistent with rural wage boom?

(a) the current status of digitization of Waqf properties across all States and Union Territories through WAMSI (Waqf Assets Management System of India) portal;
(b) the total number of Waqf properties registered and the number of properties identified as encroached upon by private or Government entities;
(c) the total revenue generated from Waqf properties nationally during the last financial year; and
(d) the legal and administrative measures proposed to expedite the eviction of illegal encroachments from statutory Waqf lands?

(a) the sanctioned cost, funding pattern and completion schedule of the Kosi-Mechi link project and the physical progress achieved; 
(b) the status of the long-pending proposal for a high dam on the Kosi in Nepal and the outcome of India-Nepal Joint Committee meetings held during 2025-26; 
(c) the amount released to the State of Bihar under the Flood Management and Border Areas Programme during the last three years against the assessed requirement; and 
(d) whether a permanent Kosi-Gandak basin authority is under consideration, given that North Bihar accounts for a disproportionate share of India’s flood-affected population year after year?

(a) the total number of Scheduled Caste (SC), Scheduled Tribe (ST) and Other Backsword Class (OBC) tenant and landless farmers in Bihar who are excluded from the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) due to the lack of digitized land ownership records;
(b) whether the Ministry has engaged with the State Government to formulate a verifiable mechanism to include landless cultivators and sharecroppers under the scheme; and
(c) the estimated economic loss suffered by marginalized farming communities in Bihar due to this structural exclusion from direct income support?

(a) the number of workers currently registered as gig or platform workers under the Code on Social Security, 2020 during the last three years, year-wise; 
(b) the average weekly earnings of gig workers in key platform sectors (home-services, delivery, ride-hailing); 
(c) the number of complaints or grievances received by the Ministry concerning wage discrimination or unequal pay among gig workers during the last two years; and
(d) the actions taken by Government to address their complaints?

(a) whether Government has compiled data on youth unemployment rates in the country during the last five years;
(b) if so, the latest youth unemployment rate (ages 18-25) and how it compares with the overall national unemployment rate;
(c) whether it is a fact that approximately 66 per cent of unemployed individuals in the country are graduates or postgraduates, as per recent labour force surveys; and
(d) if so, the specific measures taken by Government to address the skill-employment mismatch affecting educated youth?

(a) the total number of LPG connections provided under the Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana (PMUY) since its inception, State-wise;
(b) the average number of refills taken per Ujjwala beneficiary household annually during the last five years;
(c) the subsidy per LPG cylinder provided to Ujjwala beneficiaries in Financial Year 2024-25 during the same period and whether this subsidy has been revised in Financial Year 2025-26; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the reasons for Ujjwala beneficiaries taking fewer refills annually compared to non-Ujjwala households?

(a) the total number of sanctioned Professor, Associate Professor and Assistant Professor positions for SC, ST and OBC categories in Central universities as of the latest available date;
(b) the number of vacant positions in each reserved category and the percentage of vacancy compared to general category vacancies;
(c) the number of complaints of caste-based discrimination filed by SC/ST/OBC students and faculty in Central universities during the last five years, year-wise; and
(d) the number of such complaints where disciplinary action was taken against the accused and the nature of action taken?

(a) the percentage of farmers who sold their paddy and wheat at Minimum Support Price (MSP) through Government procurement during marketing seasons in the last three years, State-wise;
(b) the total value of food grain procured under MSP-linked procurement during the same period, the details thereof, State-wise; and
(c) whether Government has assessed the percentage of small and marginal farmers, as a proportion of all farmers, who are actually able to access MSP procurement?

(a) the details of Primary Health Centres (PHCs) and Community Health Centres (CHCs) operating without the mandated minimum staffing, including doctors, as per the Indian Public Health Standards (IPHS), State-wise;
(b) the number of functional PHCs providing 24x7 services, uninterrupted electricity and a continuous supply of essential medicine;
(c) the impact of non-functional primary care infrastructure on the out-of-pocket expenditure (OOPE) burden for rural households forced to access private tertiary care; and
(d) timeline for upgrading all existing PHCs to strict IPHS compliance and reallocating capital expenditure to address these foundational healthcare deficits?

(a) the total number of registered immovable Waqf properties in the country based on the latest available data;
(b) the percentage of these properties that are reported as encroached, under litigation, or of unknown status;
(c) the State-wise breakup of Waqf properties by category— mosques, graveyards, agricultural land, shops and other uses;
(d) the total estimated value of Waqf properties in the country; and
(e) the data on the number of waqf properties that have been demolished by State authorities during the last five years, State-wise?

J

(a) the number of Smart Cities selected under the Smart Cities Mission (SCM) and the total approved project cost;
(b) the number of Smart City projects that have been completed as of December, 2025 and the number that remain incomplete;
(c) the total Central and State funds released for SCM and the total expenditure incurred as of December, 2025; and
(d) whether CAG or other agencies have audited SCM implementation and if so, the findings regarding delays, cost overruns and benefit realization?

(a) district-wise data on the percentage of MGNREGA wage payments delayed beyond the statutory 15-day mandate, in Bihar during financial year 2023-24 and financial year 2024-25;
(b) total quantum of delayed compensation legally owed to workers in the State under Section 3(3) of the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) versus the amount actually disbursed;
(c) specific administrative and technical bottlenecks, including Aadhaar-Based Payment System (ABPS) mismatch errors, contributing to these persistent payment delays; and
(d) timeline for clearing all pending wage and statutory compensation arrears to mitigate rural distress and curb forced out-migration from the State?

(a) whether DoPT OM No. 28034/9/2009-Estt. (A) dated 30.09.2009 on posting of husband and wife at the same station applies to employees of Centrally funded autonomous/Statutory bodies and institutes and if not, the reasons therefor;
(b) whether any clarification/amendment is proposed to extend it to such bodies and if so, the details thereof and timeline fixed therefor; and
(c) the details regarding its applicability to autonomous/statutory bodies and in the Central Government by Central acts/rules?

(a) whether Government has taken note that the number of leprosy cases has remained above 100,000 over the last twenty years, accounting for more than 50 per cent of the global burden;
(b) if so, the reasons for the stagnation in reported cases over the years;
(c) the steps taken by Government to improve the situation;
(d) the official Government website wherefrom State-wise and district-wise leprosy data can be accessed to enable preparation of endemicity-based action plans;
(e) whether Government plans to increase budget allocation for the leprosy programme; and
(f) the details of funds allocated, released and utilised during the last three years, State/UT-wise?

(a) whether planning under  Viksit Bharat—Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB-GRAM-G) requires integration with PM Gati Shakti National Master Plan;
(b) if so, whether this centralizes decision-making that was earlier decentralized to Gram Panchayats;
(c) whether Gram Sabhas retain autonomy to decide work priorities based on local needs; and
(d) if not, whether this dilutes participatory planning mechanisms?

(a) whether Government has a Universal Social Protection plan to provide  basic level of social security for all Indian citizens;
(b) if so, the timeline and estimated budget for the initial phase of its implementation; and
(c) the funds allocated for the plan?

(a) the details of State's share in Central Taxes devolved to Bihar during financial years 2024-25 and 2025-26, compared to Budget Estimates;
(b) whether Government is aware that Bihar's Fiscal Deficit for 2024-25 rose to 9.2 per cent of GSDP at the Revised Estimate as against targeted 3 per cent, if so, the reasons for such high variance;
(c) the status of "Special Loan for Capital Expenditure" provided to Bihar in current fiscal year and the sectors where this amount has been deployed; and
(d) whether there is any proposal to increase the borrowing limit for Bihar in light of cessation of GST compensation?

(a) whether Government has identified issues in the functioning of the Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA) scheme in the last five years;
(b) the steps taken to rectify the identified issues;
(c) whether the decisions taken resulted in improvement of the functioning of the MGNREGA scheme; and
(d) if so, the details of the same and if not, the reasons for the failure?

(a) whether Government maintains data on the percentage of farmers who actually benefit from Minimum Support Price (MSP) procurement for various crops;
(b) if so, the crop-wise percentage of farmers who sold their produce at MSP during last five marketing seasons;
(c) whether it is a fact that according to research by ICAR-National Institute of Agricultural Economics & Policy Research, only 15 percent of paddy farmers and 9.6 percent of wheat farmers benefitted from MSP-backed procurement; and
(d) whether Government has assessed the reasons why 85 percent of paddy farmers, over 90 percent of wheat farmers are unable to access MSP despite it being announced as a guaranteed support price?

(a) whether Government is aware that under the National Fellowship for Scheduled Caste (NFSC), the number of fellowships awarded has remained capped at 2,000 per year despite a steady rise in SC enrolment in PhD programmes;
(b) whether it is a fact that the number of eligible applicants has consistently exceeded available slots during the last five years, leaving a large proportion of UGC-NET and CSIR-NET qualified candidates unsupported;
(c) whether the Ministry has reviewed reports of delays in disbursal of fellowship amounts to JRF and SRF under the scheme; and
(d) whether Government proposes to revise the number of NFSC fellowships and funding norms?

(a) the number of vacancies of judges in the Supreme Court and High Courts against the sanctioned strength, State-wise;
(b) the number of SC/ST/OBC judges in the Supreme Court and the percentage of representation of SCs/STs and OBCs; 
(c) the number of SC/ST/OBC judges in High Courts across the country, State-wise along with the percentage of representation of SCs/STs and OBCs;
(d) the details of criteria for sanctioning the number of posts in a district; and
(e) the year in which population was considered for sanctioning existing number of sanctioned posts?

(a) whether the Department of Personnel and Training (DoPT) permits spousal transfers for employees of autonomous bodies from one unit to another under the same Ministry;
(b) if so, the details of policy in respect of granting such permissions and the year-wise number of such transfer cases; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor and the steps being taken by Government in this regard?

(a) whether advance money for registered posts are being deposited at post offices by customers to send registered newspapers and magazines;
(b) whether there have been complaints that post offices are not sending them by registered post;
(c) whether the system of sending registered newspapers and magazines by registered posts from post offices has been discontinued; and
(d) whether a new software has been installed in the computer systems of post offices which has no provision for sending the registered newspapers and magazines?

(a) whether coverage of Pre-Matric and Post-Matric scholarship schemes for SC, ST, OBC, and minority students has declined in recent years;
(b) if so, the reasons for reduction in student beneficiaries and delay in disbursement of scholarships across States; and
(c) the impact of restricted eligibility and procedural changes on school retention and higher education enrolment among marginalised communities?

(a) the number of sanctioned posts in the subordinate judiciary across States and Union Territories, as on date;
(b) the number of judicial vacancies presently existing in such courts, category-wise;
(c) the number of cases pending before such courts, State-wise; and
(d) the timeline and mechanism fixed by Government for coordinating with States and High Courts to fill existing vacancies?

(a) whether the Minimum Wages Act is among the few labour laws that apply to both formal and informal workers;
(b) if so, whether compliance with minimum wage provisions is adequately enforced in the informal sector;  
(c) the details of enforcement mechanisms that exist under the codes to ensure minimum wage compliance across all the sectors;
(d) the number of prosecutions and penalties imposed for minimum wage violations during the last five years; and
(e) whether the wage code, once implemented, would strengthen or weaken the existing minimum wage protections?

(a) the total number of Government schools functioning in the country during the last three years, State-wise;
(b) the total student enrolment and the number of teachers employed in these schools during the same period, State-wise; 
(c) whether the Ministry maintains records on the number of schools with low or no enrolment; and
(d) if so, the criteria used for such classification?

(a) the year-wise budgetary allocation for Pariksha Pe Charcha programme during the last five years;
(b) the detailed expenditure breakup under different heads for the 2024-25 edition; 
(c) the number of students who directly participated in the programme, year-wise; and
(d) what evaluation mechanism exists to assess the impact and cost-effectiveness of the programme?

(a) whether Government investment in higher education institutions has declined in recent years;
(b) if so, the impact of such a decline on research capacity, faculty recruitment and the expansion of public universities;
(c) whether Government’s focus on foreign and private universities under NEP, 2020 risks marginalising public higher education institutions; and
(d) the steps being taken to establish new public universities, upgrade existing ones and ensure equitable access for students from rural and marginalised backgrounds?

(a) the details of the support provided by the University Grants Commission (UGC) for the establishment of Centres for Social Inclusion, including financial and academic assistance;
(b) the number of such centres currently functioning in the country, State-wise details thereof;
(c) whether it is a fact that the initiatives under this scheme have been regularly renewed every year but have not been renewed this year, if so, the reasons for non-renewal; and
(d) the details of other permanent and temporary schemes introduced or implemented by the UGC in the last five years?

(a) the latest rankings of all States, including the State of Bihar, in the NITI Aayog’s composite development index or any similar planning-based indicator;
(b) whether the State of Bihar has shown consistent improvement or decline in its planning indicators over the last five years and the reasons therefor; and
(c) specific support or planning reforms being proposed by the Central Government to assist low-performing States like Bihar?

(a) whether Government has data on the average annual income of farmers across States during the last five years;
(b) whether it is a fact that the growth in real income for small and marginal farmers remains below targets of doubling the farmers' income set by Government, if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the measures being taken to ensure substantial and sustainable increase in farmers' incomes, particularly for small and marginal farmers?

(a) the number of Gram Panchayats in Bihar that have been connected under BharatNet Phase I, II, and III as of July 2025;
(b) whether Government has identified reasons for delays in achieving full rural broadband coverage in Bihar, and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the steps being taken to expedite completion of BharatNet and ensure reliable broadband connectivity in all rural areas of Bihar within a fixed timeframe?

(a) the number of Ayushman Arogya Mandirs (AAMs) sanctioned, constructed and fully operational in Bihar as of July 2025;
(b) whether these Mandirs in Bihar are facing shortages of staff, medicines, or diagnostic tools, and the reasons for such deficiencies; and
(c) the specific steps the Ministry is taking to ensure timely staffing and availability of medicine  in Bihar’s rural and semi-urban areas?

(a) whether Government is aware that a large number of silk weavers in Bhagalpur, Bihar, have left the weaving profession due to declining orders, rising costs and lack of support;
(b) whether Government has reviewed the current status of Bhagalpur’s silk industry and the reasons for its decline, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) whether Government proposes to include Bhagalpur in the PM-MITRA Textile Parks Scheme to revive employment and improve infrastructure for weavers, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review to assess the decline in India’s press freedom rankings and the reported rise in intimidation, legal harassment and violence against journalists in recent years;
(b) whether any steps have been taken to strengthen institutional mechanisms like the Press Council of India to protect press freedom from political interference; and
(c) the measures being planned to ensure that journalists can work without fear or pressure from government or political actors?

(a) the details of number of citizens who have submitted their Aadhaar details for the purpose of linking with Voter ID, State-wise;
(b) the details of number of Voter IDs that have been linked with Aadhaar, State-wise;
(c) the details of number of voters for whom some discrepancy has been found between the details in their Aadhaar and their Voter IDs, State-wise;
(d) the procedure being followed to address such discrepancies; and
(e) the details of number of voters whose names have been taken off the voting list after linking their Aadhaar to Voter IDs, State-wise?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken note of increasing instances of student suicides reported from Higher Educational Institutions (HEIs), including IITs, Central Universities, and NITs, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether reports from these institutions regarding the causes or circumstances surrounding such incidents have been released, and if so, whether any common trends or concerns have been identified; and
(c) what measures have been taken to ensure student well-being and mental health support, and whether any monitoring mechanism exists to assess their implementation, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has disbursed the full ?2,102 crore sanctioned for MGNREGA wage payments in Bihar for the current financial year;
(b) if not, the reasons for delay or shortfall in fund release; and
(c) the corrective steps that are being taken to ensure timely wage disbursals to rural workers in Bihar, and whether social audit systems or public grievance redressal platforms have been activated in this context?

(a) total sanctioned and filled posts of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor in all Central Universities over the last five years, category-wise for SC, ST, OBC and General as of June 2025;
(b) current number of vacancies and those declared "Not Found Suitable" (NFS) in each reserved category over the last five years and whether data shows a higher NFS incidence in these categories; and
(c) the reasons for disproportionately higher NFS use in reserved-category recruitment and the corrective steps taken to ensure fair hiring of reserved category candidates?

(a) the percentage of healthcare services in the country being provided by private sector; 
(b) whether Government acknowledges the growing incidence of medical poverty in the country;
(c) the steps being taken to strengthen public health infrastructure, particularly in Bihar;
(d) whether Government has any plans to regulate costs in private hospitals and medicines to reduce dependence on private care; and
(e) whether any measures are being considered to increase public healthcare spending as a share of GDP?

(a) whether Central Government has taken steps to specifically protect the rights of consumers with disabilities under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019;
(b) whether any guidelines or mechanisms exist towards the protection of the rights of consumers with disabilities;
(c) whether the Central Government has conducted any awareness campaigns to address their specific concerns of consumers with disabilities;
(d) the number of complaints filed by consumers with disabilities before Consumer Commissions in the last three years; and
(e) whether the Central Government proposes to issue any specific rules, advisories for service providers and manufacturers to ensure non-discrimination and accessibility for disabled consumers?

(a) the number of safety and maintenance inspections conducted by the Directorate General of Civil Aviation during the last three years;
(b) the number and nature of irregularities identified during these inspections;
(c) the actions taken against airlines or operators found to be non-compliant with safety norms; 
(d) the measures being undertaken by Government to enhance aviation safety in the wake of recent concerns related to aircraft maintenance and operational standards; and
(e) whether Government plans to conduct safety audits in the aviation sector in the current year, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of slum demolitions undertaken by the Delhi Development Authority during the last three years;
(b) the total number of individuals or households displaced due to these demolitions;
(c) the number of persons rehabilitated, along with the form and location of such rehabilitation;
(d) the key challenges being faced in the rehabilitation of displaced persons;
(e) the measures being taken by the Central Government to ensure timely, adequate, and inclusive rehabilitation; and
(f) whether any budgetary allocation has been made for the purpose of rehabilitation of displaced persons, and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of vacant safety-related technical positions in the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) as of June, 2025;
(b) whether the shortage of trained aviation safety personnel has led to delays or lapses in the conduct of mandatory annual safety audits of commercial airlines and airports, and if so, the details thereof, including the last audit dates of all airlines and airports; and
(c) the steps being taken to address the staffing gap and ensuring timely and comprehensive audits in light of growing air traffic and recent safety incidents?

(a) whether Government has assessed the effectiveness of the National Monitoring Committee for Rehabilitation and Resettlement in addressing grievances related to land acquisition, compensation, and resettlement;
(b) whether there has been an increase in complaints regarding land acquisition conflicts despite the existence of this Committee, if so, the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government has established clear guidelines and timelines for resolving disputes under Article 48 of the RFCTLARR Act, 2013, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to introduce a public grievance redressal mechanism to address concerns of displaced communities in a transparent and time-bound manner?

(a) whether a large number of scientific, administrative, and technical posts are lying vacant in various Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) institutes across the country;
(b) if so, the details of such vacancies, category-wise and institute-wise, as of March 2024;
(c) whether the shortage of personnel is affecting research, administrative efficiency and overall functioning of these institutes, if not, the rationale for Government’s assessment; and
(d) the steps being taken by Government to expedite the recruitment process and ensure that all vacant positions are filled at the earliest?

(a) the reasons for not forming executive committees of said institutions in the last three years, whether administrative delays, policy decisions or any other reasons are responsible for this;
(b) whether Government is planning any special scheme to make the functioning of these institutions more effective, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether Government is planning to form a high-level committee to review the functioning of these institutions?

(a) the details of autonomous bodies related to development and promotion of various languages, under the Ministry whose Chairman is Hon'ble Minister of Education;
(b) the number of meetings of these autonomous bodies taken place under his chairmanship for promotion of various languages during 2021-22, 2022-23,2023-24 and 2024-25 till date, year-wise and autonomous body-wise;
(c) whether Government has any plan to constitute a high level committee to review their functioning; and
(d) if so, the details thereof along with other steps taken to strengthen their functioning?

(a) whether Government acknowledges that challenges such as land acquisition, difficult terrain, inclement weather and lack of proposals from States/UTs have led to delays in augmenting food grain storage capacity and strengthening Public Distribution System (PDS) operations;
(b) whether Government has considered setting key performance indicators to assess fund utilization and scheme effectiveness, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of financial proposals pending from States/UTs and the steps taken to expedite approvals; and
(d) the measures undertaken to ensure full utilization of allocated funds for food storage and PDS enhancement within the financial year?

b

(a) whether it is a fact that the coverage of beneficiaries under the National Food Security Act (NFSA) is still based on the 2011 Census;
(b) whether Government has assessed the number of additional beneficiaries who would be eligible if the coverage was updated to reflect the projected population of 2025;
(c) whether Government has taken any measures in light of the Supreme Court’s 2022 observation that benefits under NFSA should not be restricted to the 2011 Census figures; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure food security for those currently excluded due to outdated population estimates?

J

(a) whether Government has taken note of the disparity in the number of trained candidates and those receiving job offers under the National Career Services (NCS) Centres for SC/ST job seekers;
(b) the reasons for this shortfall and the corrective measures being undertaken;
(c) whether SC/ST candidates in 11 States/UTs are being excluded from the scheme’s benefits due to the absence of training centres, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure equitable access and better employment outcomes for SC/ST candidates?

b

